Title: Probe reuse of Zotero 6012 inference runtime
Created: 2026-08-30
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-08-30T16:09Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context

Zotero PR #6012 already places native ONNX inference in Firefox's separate,
memory-gated inference process. Its internal `Zotero.ML` creates engines and
manages the model cache; `Zotero.Embeddings` owns a curated model registry and
`embedQuery()` / `embedPassages()`. At PR head `77e2c4b`, the changed-file set
contains no local-API route exposing those calls, so direct reuse by an external
zoteus process appears unavailable. Confirm that boundary rather than inferring
an API from internal JavaScript names.

## Scope

Determine whether zoteus can reuse Zotero's #6012 inference process through a
supported bridge, avoiding another loaded model and another system service.
Explore an official Zotero local-API contract first. A private monkey-patch or
mandatory Zotero plugin is evidence about feasibility, not an adoption path.

## Exit criteria

- Verify against the current #6012 head whether any supported external call can
  request query and batched passage embeddings.
- If absent, specify the smallest upstream bridge: model/version identity,
  query versus passage role, batching, dimension, runtime/provider identity,
  cancellation, errors and availability. It accepts text transiently and
  exposes neither Zotero's embedding database nor arbitrary profile access.
- Test whether vectors returned by Zotero's native ONNX backend satisfy X8
  against the same registry entry used in-process; a failure keeps provider in
  vector identity.
- Compare cold-start, steady RAM, model-cache custody, version skew and failure
  behavior with in-process zoteus and a generic local endpoint.
- Record one outcome for ticket 0491: consume an existing API, propose the
  bridge upstream, defer pending #6012, or reject reuse with the blocking fact.
